From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(transfer): a slow or stray client cannot hold or
 close a local transfer; no socket off the Wi-Fi

- one connection gets a total budget for its request (DeadlineSocketInput): a peer that sent a
  byte every few seconds kept the one-connection-at-a-time server, so the offer outlived its
  two minutes and the receiver waited in the queue
- only requests that name the session (its path, a POST) and fail the proof count toward
  MAX_WRONG_REQUESTS: five GETs from anyone on the Wi-Fi used to close the offer
- receive() makes its socket off the calling thread: no Wi-Fi network is Unavailable instead of
  a request through the default route (a VPN), and a failed bindSocket no longer throws on the
  main thread

Tests: slow client, strangers cannot close the offer, bind failure; the old wrong-request test
now counts wrong proofs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
